            DIGITAL NAMES JOHN MCCLELLAND VICE PRESIDENT,
   WORLDWIDE MANUFACTURING AND LOGISTICS, FOR ITS PC BUSINESS UNIT


MAYNARD, Mass. -- January 26, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that John McClelland has joined the company as vice 
president, worldwide manufacturing and logistics, for Digital's 
Personal Computer Business Unit, effective February 1, 1995.

     McClelland, 49, will have worldwide responsibility for all 
aspects of the manufacturing and logistics functions of Digital's PC 
business, reporting to Bernhard Auer, vice president and general 
manager of Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit.

     "As one of the fastest growing PC companies in the industry, 
manufacturing and logistics play a vital role in Digital's quality 
and competitiveness," commented Auer.  "A senior executive of John's 
caliber and experience on our management team is a significant asset 
as we move up the ranks of leading companies in the PC industry."

     Prior to joining Digital, McClelland was vice president, 
worldwide manufacturing and logistics for the IBM PC Company.  
During his 26-year career at IBM, he has held a variety of executive 
management positions in IBM's manufacturing and logistics operations 
across the United Kingdom, Europe, Africa, the Middle East, and 
Asia/Pacific.  

     In addition, McClelland is a visiting professor and fellow of 
the University of Paisley in Scotland, a companion of the British 
Institute of Management, a fellow of the Royal Society of Arts, 
Manufactures and Commerce, a member of the Confederation of British 
Industry - National Manufacturing Council, a member of the Scottish 
Higher Education Funding Council, a director of the Quality Scotland 
Foundation.  In 1994 he was appointed a Commander of the Order of 
the British Empire in recognition of his contribution and services 
to education and to the advancement of British high technology 
manufacturing.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
