                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION
                             FACT SHEET


PRODUCT NAME:  DEC Network Integration Server (DECNIS) V3.0 


OVERVIEW:
    
The DECNIS V3.0 software release provides a number of new features 
for the high performance DECNIS 500/600 multiprotocol backbone 
routers.  These features greatly improve network resilience and 
redundancy in mission critical network environments. In addition, 
new hardware provides support for new high speed WAN services such 
as SMDS.


KEY FEATURES AND BENEFITS:
      

    o  Virtual Router Cluster - A group of DECNIS routers on a LAN 
       can be defined as a routing cluster in which members of the 
       cluster act as backup or standby routers to each other. 
       Virtual Router Clusters allow very fast routing recovery in 
       the event of a network failure and greatly improve resilience 
       in an IP backbone routing environment. 

    o  Resilient Routing Circuits - Allows the DECNIS to detect the 
       failure of a primary leased line routing circuit and to 
       establish a secondary, or backup, circuit only for the 
       duration of a failure, ensuring that costs are kept to a 
       minimum. Typically, primary circuits are leased line 
       circuits, while secondary circuits are ISDN or dial up 
       circuits. 

    o  Packet Prioritization - Allows different protocols or traffic 
       types to be given appropriate priority over low bandwidth WAN 
       links. For example, Telnet traffic can be prioritized over 
       FTP traffic to ensure terminal users do not suffer poor 
       screen refresh rates whilst a file transfer is taking place. 
       Also provides simple packet filtering.

    o  Pattern Matching - Allows priority packets to be further 
       classified by matching specific bit fields of packets. On the 
       basis of a match, packets can be assigned to different 
       priority queues. Provides the ability to filter bridge 
       traffic to greatly reduce network costs by stopping 
       unnecessary traffic from crossing the network.
 
    o  SMDS DXI - Switched Multi-megabit Data Service is a 
       connectionless, cell-switched data service available at 
       speeds between 56K bps and 45M bps. The DECNIS V3.0 software 
       implements SMDS DXI according to the Bellcore specification 
       and supports routing over SMDS services and can connect to 
       SMDS services at up to 16M bps Class of Service. 

    o  New Management Processor Card (MPC-II) - The new MPC-II card 
       (DNSAN-BH) provides a console port with full modem control to 
       allow out of band management from any VT100 compatible 
       terminal. The MPC-II card also has 16MB of dynamic memory for 
       storing larger routing tables and 4MB of FLASH memory for 
       storing multiple configuration files. 

    o  DEC WANcontroller 622/HS - This new high speed sync card 
       (DNSCB-B*) has two ports, each supporting line speeds at up 
       to 12Mbps. The card supports high speed connections over PPP, 
       HDLC, Frame Relay and SMDS. The DEC WANcontroller 622/HS can 
       also be connected to multiple T1/E1 lines via a single high 
       speed connection to inverse mux equipment.

    o  IPX WAN - supports native Novell IPX over leased line 
       circuits using the PPP datalink protocol but with no 
       negotiated options. This provide interoperability with other 
       router vendors' routers. 

    o  ICMP Router Discovery (RFC 1256) - allows IP hosts to 
       distinguish the DECNIS as a router using ICMP messages and 
       procedures. Using ICMP, the DECNIS periodically broadcasts 
       ICMP Router Advertisement messages and responds to ICMP 
       Router  Solicitation messages from IP Hosts. All management 
       parameters defined in  RFC 1256 are supported. 
 

PREREQUISITE HARDWARE: 
    
The DECNIS V3.0 software requires DECNIS 500 or DECNIS 600 router 
hardware. The DECNIS 500/600 provide high performance multiprotocol 
routing and bridging and are modular, expandable  platforms which 
use a variety of LAN and WAN interface cards to connect to network 
services. 


PREREQUISITE SOFTWARE: 
    
The DECNIS V3.0 Software is installed and configured on a standard 
MS-DOS PC, OpenVMS/VAX or DEC OSF/1 AXP system and then loaded into 
the DECNIS FLASH memory using BOOTP or MOP over LAN or WAN 
connections.


PRICING AND AVAILABILITY:
    
The DECNIS 500/600 hardware prices are as follows:


    DECNIS 500, MPC-II, memory card, 2 slots	    $ 6,600
    DECNIS 600, MPC-II, memory card. 7 slots	    $13,900
    DEC LANcontroller 602, 2 port Ethernet	    $ 4,800
    DEC WANcontroller 622, 2 port T1/E1		    $ 4,200
    DEC WANcontroller 618, 8 port DS0		    $ 7,000
    DEC FDDIcontroller 621, 1 port FDDI, SAS/DAS    $12,500    

    NEW DEC WANcontroller 622/HS, 2 port, 12Mbps    $ 7,500
    NEW DECNIS MPC-II, 16MB DRAM/4MB FLASH, console $ 6,500


The DECNIS V3.0 software is priced separately and includes all 
software functions and features:

    DECNIS VAX/VMS TK50 Media and Doc Kit	    $   450
    DECNIS OSF/1 for AXP CDROM and Doc Kit	    $   450
    DECNIS DOS RX23 Media and Doc Kit		    $   250

    
The DECNIS V3.0 software and the new DECNIS MPC-II and DEC 
WANcontroller 622/HS cards are available now.
