             DIGITAL TO PROVIDE MEDIA SERVER TECHNOLOGY
                      FOR AMERITECH DEPLOYMENT


   Digital's Media Server Platform To Deliver Interactive Services
              to Millions of Homes in Mid-Western U.S.


MAYNARD, Mass. -- February 21, 1995 -- In preparation for the 
largest mass-market deployment of interactive video services to 
date, Digital Equipment Corporation and Ameritech announced that 
they have signed a broad-based technology agreement, under which 
Digital will provide its media server platform for Ameritech's 
interactive services deployment. Today's agreement will provide 
Digital with as much as $40 million in product and service revenues 
over the next five years.

     Digital's media servers platform will be a central component of 
Ameritech's new network that will deliver movies-on-demand, home-
shopping and other interactive entertainment services.  The 
Ameritech network is expected to become operational in the first 
midwestern communities by the end of this year.

     According to Sultan Zia, general manager of Digital's Video and 
Interactive Information Services group, "The combination of 
Digital's high-performance media servers and Ameritech's networking 
expertise will change the way millions of consumers spend at-home 
leisure time -- shopping, accessing information and watching 
movies."  Zia added that by eliminating trials and moving directly 
to deployments, Ameritech is accelerating the delivery of available 
interactive video services and increasing the need for programming. 
"In anticipating larger markets for their programs, content 
providers will produce content sooner, thereby providing consumers 
with more choices and creating more demand."

     Digital's media server platform has already been selected by 
more cable and telephone companies worldwide than any other video 
server provider. The company's Video and Interactive Information 
Architecture provides a full-service solution for delivering 
interactive video applications over many types of networks. 
Currently the industry's only second-generation media server, 
Digital's platform features object-oriented middleware that links 
the world's fastest server systems -- based on 64-bit Alpha 
processors -- with the company's StorageWorks disk arrays and 
digital tape library systems.  This architecture also provides 
network, subscriber, and billing management capabilities in an open 
framework that supports third-party and legacy applications.

     Ameritech (NYSE: AIT), one of the world's largest 
communications companies, provides local phone, data and video 
services for more than 13 million customers in Illinois, Indiana, 
Michigan, Ohio, and Wisconsin. The company is currently developing 
new information, entertainment and interactive services for homes, 
businesses and governments worldwide. Nearly 1 million investors 
hold Ameritech shares.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry- 
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
