        DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION AND SAP AG FORM STRATEGIC
              PARTNERSHIP TO FOCUS ON THE PROCESS INDUSTRY


              Digital dedicates more than 100 consultants 
                 exclusively to the process industry


WALLDORF, GERMANY and MAYNARD, MASS. -- February 13, 1995 -- SAP AG, 
the world's leading provider of client/server business applications 
today announced a strategic partnership with Digital Equipment 
Corporation to dedicate combined resources to the process industry. 
To serve the specific needs of this market, Digital has formed a 
team of more than 100 worldwide consultants with extensive knowledge 
in the process areas of pharmaceuticals, chemical, consumer packaged 
goods, semi-conductor, and oil industries (specialty lubricants and 
chemicals divisions). The alliance is dedicated to providing 
services for the complex requirements of process industry customers.

     "This partnership will allow both Digital and SAP to further forge 
out way into the process industry. By uniting with industry and 
technology specialists we can develop the focused solutions that our 
customers are looking for, and increase support by providing more 
consultants with specific expertise in the MES (Manufacturing Execution
Systems)" explains Paul Whal, Senior Vice President, SAP AG.

     The SAP/Digital relationship in the process industry began with the 
CAPISCE (Computer Architecture for Production Information Systems in a
Competitive Environment) project. CAPISCE was a consortium of various
companies - SAP, Digital, ICI/Zeneca, IDS Prof, Scheer GmbH and
Institut for Wirtschattsinformatik which had been established to 
combine applications development and practical industry knowledge to 
develop general purpose solution to satisfy process manufacturers' 
demands for flexible response to market changes. SAP's contribution is
its R/3 module called PP-PI (an open solution for production planning
in process industries) while Digital provided PDAS (Process Data
Acquisition System), the first third-party product Integrated to PP-PI
and certified by SAP.

     PDAS, and open solution, integrates the execution planned by PP-PI 
for the automation, control equipment, and complimentary solutions 
typically found in the process manufacturing execution environment. In
addition to the consultants dedicated to PP-PI consulting and 
implementation, Digital will utilize existing resources to provide PDAS
consultancy.

     Paul Van der Spiegel, Vice President, Systems Integration, Digital 
Europe, explains, "our alliance support to customers is even greater 
with this agreement because together we can expand our range of focused
products and solutions for the process industries." The CAPISCE
project has shown the impact that dedicated resources have on industry
specific requirements. The customer will benefit from this strategic
relationship, which unites Digitals long association with process
manufacturers in the IMES (Integrated Manufacturing Execution Systems)
area, with SAP's integrated client/server based software and
complimentary network of resources and products available from Digital
and SAP partners.

     PP-PI and PDAS are now implemented in ZENECA and are already 
improving Zeneca's performance measurements. SAP and Digital are 
engaged in additional pilots for both PP-PI and PDAS with customers 
across the process industries.

About SAP

     SAP provides flexible, integrated client/server and mainframe-based 
business applications software that is compatible with most popular 
hardware, software and database platforms. More than 4,000 companies
in 41 countries use SAP software to manage complex financial,
manufacturing, sales and human resource requirements. Founded in 1972,
SAP AG is headquartered in Walldorf, Germany and employs a workforce of
over 5,000 worldwide. SAP America is the largest of SAP's 30 global
subsidiaries and affiliates. SAP America is comprised of its corporate
headquarters in Philadelphia, a Technology Development Center in Foster
City, California, and sales support offices throughout North America.

About Digital

     Systems Integration is an area where Digital is well-respected. 
Over the past several years, the corporation has been ranked among the
top five integrators in the world. Digital's Systems Integration
business provides solutions which align technology in support of
customers' business needs by integrating Digital and third-party
products and services, and providing project and consulting services,
and providing project and consulting services in targeted technologies,
applications and industry domains. The core competencies of Digital's
Systems Integration are Information Technology Consulting, Applications
and Data Integration and Integrating Systems.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open client/
server solutions from personal computing to integrated worldwide 
information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, storage, 
networking, software and services, together with industry-focused 
solutions from business partners, help organizations compete and win in
today's global marketplace. 
