        DIGITAL EXPANDS LINE OF STORAGEWORKS TAPE SUBSYSTEMS
           TO ADDITIONAL UNIX AND PC NETWORK ENVIRONMENTS


       Digital's Storage Business Unit Also Announces Extended
               Third Party Software Management Support


MAYNARD, Mass. -- February 21, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today expanded its line of multivendor tape backup solutions by 
announcing expanded support for Sun, IBM, Hewlett-Packard, Windows 
NT, Novell and Digital computing platforms.  Digital now offers 
seamless integration of 4 mm DDS2, 8 mm and Digital Linear Tape 
(DLT) technologies that can be mixed and matched in any StorageWorks 
enclosure with other StorageWorks devices, including disk and CD-ROM 
drives, across the multivendor environment.

     Also today, Arcada Software and Legato Systems, Inc. separately 
announced software management support for StorageWorks tape 
subsystems.  Arcada Backup Exec now supports all StorageWorks tape 
drives and autoloaders for both Alpha and Intel based Windows NT, as 
well as Novell NetWare.  Legato NetWorker now supports most 
StorageWorks tape drives on Sun Solaris, SunOS, Novell NetWare, and 
IBM AIX.  Earlier this year, Legato Systems and Digital announced 
new functionality and new clientside archiving support for 
POLYCENTER NetWorker Save and Restore for DEC OSF/1 Alpha.

     "These new StorageWorks tape offerings reflect our commitment 
to support users in as many environments as possible with reliable 
and high performing tape backup solutions," stated Paul Feresten, 
vice president of sales and marketing for Digital's Storage Business 
Unit.  "Our customers are increasingly operating in multivendor 
environments and are demanding flexible storage solutions with 
cross-platform capabilities.  And because storage management 
software is integral to successful data management, we're working 
aggressively to ensure partnerships are in place with 
industry-leading software providers to support StorageWorks 
products."  Feresten added that new support from Arcada and Legato 
complements existing partnerships with Cheyenne and Palindrome.

New Tape Offerings and Availability

     With a wide range of tape technology choices, StorageWorks tape 
subsystems offer a variety of DLT, 8 mm, and 4 mm backup solutions 
for Sun, Hewlett-Packard and IBM UNIX platforms, Novell NetWare and 
Windows NT Intel PC network platforms, and Digital platforms, 
including Windows NT Alpha.  New offerings include:

Digital Linear Tape (DLT)

     The StorageWorks line of DLT tape solutions now supports IBM 
UNIX and Hewlett-Packard 9000 Series 700 UNIX platforms, making the 
product line available for all major vendor platforms.  Digital 
supports the products across major PC Network and UNIX platforms 
through partnerships with a range of third-party network backup 
companies, including Arcada, Cheyenne, Legato Systems, and 
Palindrome. These DLT offerings feature unattended backup with 
industry-leading capacities (20 GB per cartridge with compression) 
and a superior sustained data transfer rate (up to 2.5 MB per second).  
Pricing is $4,399.

DLT Mini-Library

     With this announcement, the line of StorageWorks DLT Mini-
Libraries is now available on Sun Solaris, SunOS, and Windows NT 
platforms, in addition to existing availability on Novell NetWare, 
with support from Legato NetWorker and Arcada Backup Exec.  The 
compact, five-cartridge mini-library features 100 GB storage 
capacity, while the seven-cartridge mini-library is rack-mountable, 
or available in a pedestal, and features 140 GB of storage capacity.  
Prices start at $8,289.

8 mm Tape

     The StorageWorks line of 8 mm tape offerings now includes 
support for Hewlett-Packard HP-UX users, making the storage backup 
solutions available for all major vendor platforms.  This tape 
option provides high performance and capacity (10 GB per drive with 
compression) at an affordable price, ranging from $2,790 - $2,950.

4 mm DDS-2 Tape

     Finally, to round out its 4 mm DDS-2 tape offerings, 
StorageWorks has added support for IBM UNIX users, making the 
product line available for all major vendor platforms.  These 
low-cost storage solutions provide reliable backup (up to 2.9 GB of 
data per hour) and capacities up to 8 GB for prices starting at 
$1,999.

4 mm (DDS2) Autoloader

     Also as part of this announcement, the StorageWorks 4mm DDS2 
Autoloader now supports users on Windows NT, and NetWare platforms.  
This product is also available for the first time under a separate 
part number for Digital OpenVMS and OSF/1 platforms.  The 
StorageWorks 32 GB (with compression) DAT tape loader mounted in 
5.25-inch building block is priced  from $3,950 - $4,150.
All prices are effective on March 1, 1995.

     The StorageWorks line of tape solutions is sold exclusively 
through channel partners worldwide, including VARs, distributors, 
master resellers, and system integrators.  StorageWorks products for 
Digital platforms and operating environments are also available 
directly from the Digital sales force.

     StorageWorks is a comprehensive family of disk, tape and 
optical storage subsystems, offering modular, competitively-priced, 
industry-standard solutions in customizable desktop, deskside and 
datacenter enclosures.  StorageWorks products are available on 
multiple operating systems and hardware platforms, including Novell 
and Windows NT environments, Digital workstations and midrange 
computers, and Hewlett-Packard, IBM, and Sun workstations and 
servers.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
