                   DIGITAL ANNOUNCES NEW FEATURES
                      FOR UNIX OPERATING SYSTEM


  ...DEC OSF/1 leads industry in network performance; UNIX systems
                   sales show impressive growth...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- February 22, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced a new release of the DEC OSF/1 operating system with 
advanced networking and software development features. Support for 
ATM protocols provide users with access to high performance networks 
for faster access to data and applications, while the new CDE 
developers kit and improved software debugging tools allow faster 
development of next-generation applications.

     The new features are expected to continue the growth of 
Digital's UNIX business.  "International Data Corp. is right on 
target with their estimates of 71% growth in UNIX business overall," 
said Don Harbert, vice president of Digital's UNIX Business Unit. 
"That's the highest growth rate in the industry. Our Alpha business 
on UNIX has more than doubled over last year and the growth trend is 
continuing." 

     "Digital has thousands of UNIX workstations and servers in use 
around the world, with well over 1,000,000 users, added Harbert.  
"We have supported customers running UNIX from its very inception."

     Digital will ship DEC OSF/1 V3.2 for the Alpha platform later 
this month.  DEC OSF/1 V3.2 software is available for Alpha systems 
from the DEC 3000 Model 300LX five thousand dollar workstation 
through the DEC 7000 family of enterprise servers with up to six 
processors and 14 Gbytes of memory.  Version 3.2 also supports 
cluster configurations such as AdvantageCluster Available Server 
3000 and the AdvantageCluster Compute Server 5000. 

Latest version of UNIX supports fastest network performance

     A major new feature is support for the Asynchronous Transfer 
Mode (ATM ) network protocol.  DEC OSF/1 now not only supports 
conventional networking protocols such as TCP/IP, but also delivers 
industry-leading performance on emerging networking technologies 
such as ATM through Digital's ATMworks 750 TURBOchannel adapter. 

     "We tested available ATM adapters on HP, SGI, and Sun systems, 
and none came close to Digital's ATMworks adapters in performance,"  
said Dirk Grunwald, Assistant Professor of Computer Science at the 
University of Colorado at Boulder.  "We measured more than 
130Mbits/sec. using TCP/IP from DEC OSF/1.  Installation and 
management was also much simpler than with ATM on other platforms." 

     Also included with the new release is improved management 
support with Networker SingleServer Save and Restore, the industry 
leading graphical utility.  The utility provides fully automated, 
unattended backup and recovery of files on a single local system to 
a local tape or loader. 

Development tools for desktop interface, system management tools 
for peak application performance

     Included with Version 3.2 is Digital's advanced development kit 
for the Common Desktop Environment (CDE), the emerging standard user 
environment embraced by all of the leading UNIX vendors.  Developers 
can begin their work to deploy applications for the new environment 
now and be ready to ship their applications when a full production 
release of CDE is available later this year. 

     Version 3.2 includes enhancements for symmetric multiprocessing 
(SMP) environments.  The enhancements allow system managers to take 
individual processors off-line and place them on-line without taking 
the system down, and to reserve and dedicate a set of processors to 
a specific task. An enhanced debugger is included which supports 
application development and debugging of SMP application code. 

     DEC OSF/1 V3.2 software is binary compatible with DEC OSF/1 
V3.0, allowing Digital software and third party applications 
presently running on V3.0 to run without modification.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
