              INDUSTRY WATCHER MELLING JOINS DIGITAL AS
              VICE PRESIDENT, OPENVMS SYSTEMS BUSINESS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- February 22, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced that Wesley Melling will join the company as vice 
president, OpenVMS Systems Business, reporting to Jesse Lipcon, vice 
president, Systems Business Group, effective March 6. Melling joins 
Digital from the Gartner Group, consultants to the information 
technology industry, where he was Program Director for Midrange 
Computing Strategies.

     Melling, 56, will be responsible for growing the OpenVMS 
business, revenue and profitability. OpenVMS is one of Digital's key 
operating system solutions, with over one million users to date. 

     "Wes is uniquely suited for this role, having 'industry-
watched' Digital over the past four years at Gartner Group, and 
having been in frequent contact with many of our largest customers," 
commented Lipcon. "His strategic background, forecasting 
capabilities, special consulting expertise in the areas of open 
systems, mission-critical transaction processing, and the 
development of enterprise information architectures will be welcome 
in the OpenVMS business, the Systems Business Group, and the entire 
corporation."

     Prior to the Gartner Group, Melling was senior vice president 
of Information Resource Management at Ingram Distribution Group, a 
book and video distributor. Previously, he was vice president, MIS, 
at HealthAmerica Corporation.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
