                  NEW ENTRY-LEVEL ALPHA WORKSTATION
                    IS PRICE/PERFORMANCE LEADER;
           VOLUME SALES EXPECTED THROUGH CHANNEL PARTNERS


MAYNARD, Mass. -- February 23, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today unveiled a new entry-level, 64-bit AlphaGeneration workstation 
-- the AlphaStation 200 4/100 workstation. The workstation is a 
price/performance leader and will be popular with customers who want 
an inexpensive but powerful system running the UNIX operating 
system. 

     The system supports three operating systems -- DEC OSF/1 
(Digital's version of UNIX), Windows NT, and OpenVMS -- so customers 
can choose the application and operating system best suited to run 
their businesses. The system also incorporates the high-performance 
PCI bus--a standard in the PC industry that enables customers to 
purchase a wide range of peripherals from the thousands of vendors 
who service the PC market. 

     "With the new systems, Digital continues to offer workstations 
with the best price/performance of any comparable systems on the 
market," said Philippe Ribeyre, vice president, Alpha Workstation 
Business Segment.  "The new workstation provides extraordinary value 
by combining high-end performance with low-cost design features." 

Volume Sales through Channels Partners

     Digital will sell the workstations directly, and in volume 
through its channel partners. Digital's channel partners are 
enthusiastic about selling the new products. For example, Robert 
Braverman, vice president, marketing, Avnet Computer, said "Digital 
has been cooperative in working with its partners. Digital has also 
priced its new products in a way that benefits us, and has 
advertised the systems widely to build demand. People are regarding 
Digital as the price/performance leader in the workstation and 
server markets. Avnet is seeing a double-digit increase in sales of
Digital's products over last year." 

Fastest Low-Cost Workstation

     With CPU performance of 100 MHz, and SPECint92 and SPECfp92
performance of 74.59 and 95.23 respectively, the AlphaStation 200 
4/100 workstation offers customers up to twice the performance of 
entry-level competitive workstations. 

     It supports leading applications in technical markets, 
including MCAD, ECAD, GIS, and CASE; and commercial markets, 
including desktop publishing, office productivity, and database 
applications. 
     
Outstanding Investment Protection

     "With the new workstation, customers can rest assured that 
their computing investments in Digital's systems are protected," 
added Ribeyre. "Digital will offer inexpensive upgrades as new and 
more powerful CPU chips are introduced to meet customers' needs." 

     The system comes with an industry leading, three-year warranty 
featuring on-site service with next-day response for the first year. 

Pricing and Availability

     The AlphaStation 200 4/100 workstation is priced at $4,991 for 
a system with a 1.05 GByte disk, 32 MBytes of memory, and the DEC 
OSF/1 or OpenVMS operating systems. An AlphaStation 200 4/100 with 
the Windows NT Workstation operating system, a 340 Mbyte disk, and 
16 MBytes of memory is priced at $4,285. 

     The AlphaStation 200 4/100 workstation is currently available 
and shipping. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace. 
