               DIGITAL NAMES O'DONNELL VICE PRESIDENT,
           QUALITY AND CUSTOMER SERVICES, PC BUSINESS UNIT


MAYNARD, Mass. -- February 23, 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today named Arthur J. O'Donnell, vice president, Quality and 
Customer Services for Digital's Personal Computer Business Unit, 
reporting to Bernhard Auer, vice president and general manager of 
the PC business unit.

     In his multi-dimensional role, O'Donnell, 48, is focused on 
customer satisfaction and product/service cost competitiveness.  His 
responsibilities include worldwide establishment, implementation and 
maintenance of a quality system across all PC business functions.  
In addition, he is responsible for the development and management of 
a comprehensive customer service and support capability, as well as 
managing the warranty budget on behalf of the product lines.

     "Customer satisfaction is a top priority at Digital," said 
Auer.  "Art was instrumental in building Digital's Multivendor 
Customer Services Business, which is rated among the best in the 
industry.  His successes with that organization make him the ideal 
candidate to lead this effort for Digital's PC business."

     O'Donnell joined Digital in 1974 and has an extensive 
background in services and quality management.  Most recently he was 
vice president of Digital's Multivendor Customer Services Hardware 
Systems Business.

     O'Donnell is a graduate of Framingham State College and Boston 
University's Development Program.  He received his MBA from 
Northeastern University.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
