        TIVOLI SYSTEMS INC. AND DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION
   TO PORT TIVOLI MANAGEMENT ENVIRONMENT TO DIGITAL'S UNIX SYSTEMS


   ... Digital's UNIX Customers to implement Tivoli's distributed
                  client/server management software


MAYNARD, Mass. -- February, 24 1995 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
and Tivoli Systems Inc. today announced they have agreed to port the 
Tivoli Management Environment (TME) to Alpha systems running 
Digital's UNIX, the DEC OSF/1 operating system.  The TME suite of 
system management applications for the Alpha family is targeted to 
ship in May 1995. 

     "The addition of TME tools for system management is excellent 
news for our customers," said Don Harbert, vice president, UNIX 
Systems Business for Digital.  "A strong administrative environment 
is a key element in the operation of large distributed computing 
resources and Tivoli technology delivers what many customers need."

     "Our agreement reinforces three major elements of Digital's 
UNIX strategy," Harbert added. "First, it enhances our ability to 
deliver complete commercial computing solutions to our customers 
world-wide; second, it expands our ability to deliver quality UNIX 
system management capabilities that fit diverse customer 
requirements; and third, it is another example of business 
partnerships that create powerful solutions for the UNIX customers 
we share." 

     "One of Tivoli's key business strategies is to provide an open, 
heterogeneous systems management solution," said Russ Caccamisi, 
vice president of marketing for Tivoli Systems Inc.  "Clearly, 
Digital has significant presence in the marketplace and we are 
pleased to offer our solution on their platform." 

     The Tivoli Management Environment provides a comprehensive set 
of systems management applications that reduce the cost and mask the 
complexity of managing widely dispersed UNIX and PC clients and 
servers.  The TME provides key client/server systems management 
applications addressing both deployment and operations functions 
such as software distribution, client and server configuration 
management and event monitoring and correlation.  The Tivoli 
Management Framework (TMF) provides an architectural foundation 
within the TME on which to build and run highly integrated and 
easy-to-use systems management applications and has been widely 
accepted as an industry standard. 

     Tivoli Systems Inc. is a leading supplier of systems management 
software and services for the client/server market and an 
acknowledged technology pioneer in this emerging industry. 
Headquartered in Austin, Texas, Tivoli distributes its products 
worldwide through a network of domestic and international sales 
offices, international distributors and systems integrators. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions, from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
