                TOP SOFTWARE DEVELOPMENT TOOL VENDORS
             EXPAND SOLUTIONS ALLIANCE TO NORTH AMERICA


   ...SEE IT Alliance Forges Cooperative Development Solutions...


MAYNARD, Mass. -- February 24, 1995 -- Nine of the world's leading 
vendors of software development tools and development environments 
today jointly announced the formation of a North American chapter of 
the SEE IT Alliance.  The SEE IT Alliance, now with chapters in 
Europe and North America, was established in October 1994 to deliver 
integrated solutions for multivendor software development programs.  
The SEE IT Alliance focuses on building, marketing, and supporting 
customer-driven, open-systems solutions for software engineering 
teams worldwide.

     The North American partners in the SEE IT Alliance and their 
respective software development products include:

     * 	Atria Software Inc. (ClearCase and ClearCase MultiSite)
     *  Cadre Technologies Inc. (Teamwork and ObjectTeam)
     * 	Digital Equipment Corporation (COHESIONworX and COHESION
     	Team/SEE)
     * 	Digital Tools (AutoPLAN II)
     * 	Electronic Data Systems (EDS), Inc. (PORTOS)
     * 	i-Logix Inc (Statemate)
     *  Interleaf, Inc. (Interleaf 6)
     *  Rational Software Corporation (Rational Apex and VADS 
        compiler technology)
     * 	SQL Software Ltd. (PCMS)

     Together, these products provide flexible, open, integrated 
software development solutions that support transparent distribution 
of data and tools across client/server networks of UNIX platforms 
from different vendors.

Members Cite Need for Alliance

     Mory Bahar, Cadre's vice president of marketing, said, "The SEE 
IT Alliance allows customers to benefit from the best that many 
vendors have to offer.  Through integration with other tools and 
compatibility with various UNIX platforms, customers are able to 
choose the tools they want to work with from leading vendors, 
knowing that the tools all work together to provide a complete 
software development solution."

     Elwyn Wareham, sales manager, Advanced Technology and Products 
Group, EDS Defence, stressed the critical nature of software 
engineering programs to many organizations and activities.

     "Air traffic control systems must expand and modernize to cope 
with increasing congestion, financial service companies must evolve 
to support new business models, and communications systems must 
exploit new satellite and switching technologies," Wareham said.  
"These are just a few examples of areas where disciplined software 
engineering, supported by the SEE IT Alliance, is essential."

Open Systems Support

     "Companies that are developing large or complex software 
systems require a robust set of integrated development tools in 
order to remain competitive and manage risk," said Tom Smith, 
strategic account manager, Rational Software Corporation.  "As an 
active member of the SEE IT Alliance, Rational will continue to 
support open systems, industry standards, and interoperability 
between the leading software-engineering tools."

     Tani Haque, CEO of SQL Software Ltd., said.  "In software 
engineering there is a significant difference between a marginally 
functional, difficult-to-maintain, poorly documented software 
application and one that is functionally robust, reliable, easily 
maintained and well documented. The SEE IT Alliance provides the 
means that enable software engineers to apply their skills and 
creativity to their work.  This is a true key to productivity."

Customer-Centered Solutions

     Development and evolution of the SEE IT Alliance's integrated 
solutions will be continually driven by customer input.  All aspects 
of customer needs are considered, from business relationships and 
support to technical requirements.  Within the alliance, partners 
cooperate to design and deliver off-the-shelf and customized 
solutions to meet specific customer requirements.  Each partner 
retains final responsibility for selling and supporting their 
respective products.

     Daryll Shatz, Digital's Software Engineering Marketing Alliance 
manager, pointed out that SEE IT Alliance members have helped many 
companies raise the efficiency of their software development 
programs.  A goal of the alliance is to help all customers reach 
Level 3 of the Carnegie-Mellon Software Engineering Institute's 
five-level scale for software engineering process maturity.

    Shatz believes that the strong relationships among the partners 
in the SEE IT Alliance is key to the stability and maturity that 
developers are looking for.  Shatz went on to express his view that 
by including the developers in the evolution of their environment, 
the alliance gives small to large development teams the confidence 
that the technology they are using has a long life and that their 
investment is secure.

Complementary Solutions

     Robert Parker, vice president of marketing at Atria, said, "We 
look forward to being an active members of the SEE IT alliance and 
offering developers comprehensive and adaptable software solutions.  
The SEE IT Alliance strongly complements our fundamental business 
model, which is to provide best-of-breed, open development solutions 
that adapt to individual developer needs and strengthen the entire 
development team."

Multiplatform Desktop Environment

     SEE IT solutions support software development in C, C++, 
Fortran, Ada, and Pascal programming languages, and are available 
for hardware platforms running the SunOS, HP/UX and DEC OSF/1 
operating systems.  Digital's COHESIONworX software, a distributed, 
client/server, multivendor development environment, is the 
integration technology for SEE IT solutions.  SEE IT Alliance 
members offer complementary solutions that include requirements 
traceability, systems analysis and design, configuration management, 
prototyping/simulation, project planning and management, software 
metrics, and documentation management.

     Using an object-oriented, graphical desktop interface, software 
developers build customizable "work areas" to invoke tools and 
access project data.  The desktop environment enables software 
developers to integrate existing tools and add new tools easily, 
without tool modification or desktop reconfiguration.  Once 
integrated, a tool can be accessed from the desktop work area and 
interact with other tools anywhere in the client/server network.  
This ability to distribute tool access and operation across a 
multivendor network preserves a customer's existing investments in 
software tools, hardware, and training.

Industry Standards, Integrated Services

     SEE IT solutions derive their multivendor network support 
capability from implementation of industry standards, including the 
Motif graphical user interface and DCE (Distributed Computing 
Environment) from the Open Software Foundation;  the Object 
Management Group's Common Object Request Broker Architecture 
(CORBA);  PCTE (Portable Common Tool Environment);  X3H6;  and 
evolving COSE (Common Open Software Environment) specifications.

     "The SEE IT Alliance also has integrated key education, 
consulting, and support services from each of its partners," said Al 
Olsen, manager of Digital's Software Engineering Marketing group.  
"The integration of  the core environment, code development tools, 
and services has produced a set of flexible solutions for small 
development teams as well as very large programming efforts spanning 
many organizations, and delivered anywhere in the world.

     "These solutions are available today from SEE IT Alliance 
partners and run on UNIX platforms from Digital, Sun and 
Hewlett-Packard," Olsen added.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
