              FARRAHAR ANNOUNCES PLANS TO LEAVE DIGITAL


MAYNARD, Mass. -- January 31, 1995 -- Richard M. Farrahar, vice 
president of Human Resources, today announced his intention to leave 
his position at Digital Equipment Corporation, effective at the end 
of the corporation's fiscal year in June.

     Farrahar, 50, joined Digital in 1970 as a recruiter in the 
Sales and Services organization. During his tenure, he has held a 
number of group and regional Human Resources positions. In 1988, he 
became vice president of Personnel for Manufacturing, Engineering 
and Product Marketing and in 1989, he was promoted to vice president 
of Human Resources.

     Robert B. Palmer, Digital's president and chief executive 
officer, commented, "Dick has made many contributions to Digital and 
its culture, both during the company's growth and in this current 
period of turnaround. His particular interest in the development of 
a diverse workforce as a competitive business advantage and in the 
development of human resource management professionals for the 
future will stand as a lasting contribution to Digital.

     "During the next five months, Dick will continue with his 
current responsibilities and participate in the search for a new 
vice president of Human Resources," continued Palmer.

     "My years at Digital have been great ones," said Farrahar. 
"They have been filled with learning, fun and opportunities to 
contribute.  I have reached a personal decision that now is the 
right time for me, the Human Resources function and Digital to make 
this change and I am looking forward to the opportunity, after June, 
to pursue new challenges."

