                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION REDOUBLES
                        ITS COMMITMENT TO THE WIRELESS
                          TELECOMMUNICATIONS INDUSTRY

         
             "A World Without Boundaries" Unveiled at Wireless '95

         
NEW ORLEANS, LA -- February 1, 1995 -- Digital Equipment 
Corporation today unveiled "A World Without Boundaries" at 
the Cellular Telecommunications Industry Association's (CITA) 
Wireless '95 at the Ernest N. Morial Convention Center in New 
Orleans, Louisiana in booth #1754.  Digital and its wireless 
industry partners, InfoCellular, Inc., Kingston-SCL, MPR 
Teltech Ltd., Metrica, SAP and SEMA Group Telecom demonstrate 
their leading wireless solutions making the toughest problems 
faced by cellular providers easy to solve.
         
     "We are excited to be here in New Orleans," said Scott Kane, 
Digital's director of Telecommunications for the Americas.  
"In the last twelve months Digital has redoubled its effort 
and investment in the wireless telecommunications industry 
and we are quickly seeing the payoff.  We have recently 
signed agreements with three leading partners, Kingston SCO, 
Ltd., MPR Teltech Ltd., and SEMA Group, significantly 
expanding our product offerings.  Moreover, we have added 
important new customers and installations around the globe, 
both directly and through our partners.  Some of these 
include Cellcom, TAC Worldphone, E-Plus and Hutchison 
Microtel (Orange)."
         
     "We are pleased to be partnering with Digital," Vince 
Holloway, senior director of Network Operation Support 
Systems for MPR Teltech, said.  "MPR's market research and 
experience confirms that the communications market is moving 
from proprietary Network Management platforms to 
standards-based platforms.  For the past three years, MPR has 
provided standards-based applications for Digital's TeMIP 
software, and our newly signed agreement with Digital 
confirms MPR's further commitment to open solutions to meet 
our customer's needs."
         
     Digital's exhibit demonstrates leading wireless technology 
designed to save cellular providers and subscribers time and 
money.  With its technology, cellular providers are able to 
introduce new services and build and integrate network 
management solutions more quickly; fraud and cloning are 
easier to detect; billing information is more quickly 
analyzed and new services more easily identified and 
introduced.  The bottom line is more cost-efficient and 
productive operations for cellular providers and operators.

Digital Equipment Corporation, Leading the Industry With the 
Right Partners and Solutions
         
Customer Care and Billing
         
     Digital's high-performance 64-bit Alpha Systems together with 
Kingston-SCL's, Jupiter billing system is benchmarked for 
multimillion subscriber performance.  Jupiter is one of the 
world's leading administration, billing, and customer care 
solutions.  Advanced system design lets operators run 
multiple networks -- PCs, cellular, paging, fixed and more -- 
all in one billing system.
         
     Digital's partner Sema Group Telecom, is a leading-edge 
provider of billing and customer service solutions for the 
wireless industry.  Sema Group Telecom offers applications 
for the seamless control of this critical interface between 
the customer and the network operator.  CABS 2000 is the 
culmination of the Sema Group's global experience in building 
cellular systems designed to support the cellular operator 
through changing business needs and growing subscriber 
levels. CABS 2000 offers a product-based upgrade path, but 
can also be customized as needed.  It is a proven system, 
operational in installations worldwide and can be used in 
either GSM or non-GSM operations.
         
Network Management
         
     Digital covers every aspect of network management with three 
complementary solutions:
         
         1)  Digital's TeMIP software for network management
         2)  Metrica's Network Performance Reporting
         3)  MPR Teltech's expertise in complex system integration
         
Digital's TeMIP, a solutions platform as well as a framework, 
makes building and integrating public network management 
solutions quicker and easier.  Based on a client/server 
approach, it allows the deployment of both distributed and 
hierarchical solutions.  TeMIP and its toolkits are designed 
to allow fast introduction of new technologies and new 
services, while integrating the management of existing 
services.  It provides an operational staff with 
comprehensive network monitoring and control capabilities.
         
     The Metrica Network Performance Reporting system from 
Metrica, Inc., is a single integrated set of tools that let 
network operators collect, store and analyze months of 
performance data from cells, switches, and other network 
elements.  Point-and-click choices let operators visualize 
usage trends over time, report on cell or switch load, and 
forecast growth or change in network capacity.
         
     MPR Teltech, Ltd., is a systems integrator specializing in 
